Symmetric (Galerkin) volumetric pairing, selected by the deck.

THE PAIRING IS A DECK PROPERTY, NOT A BUILD OPTION.  fbares.py --symmetric
emits U3 types whose third label character is '_' instead of the ring letter
LETTERS[nring-1]; mastruct.c and mafillsmas.f must not decode that marker
(95-65+1 = 31 would silently clamp the row loop), and e_c3d_u3.f assembles
the Galerkin form

    K_vol = (K V_h) sbar^T sbar

over the whole E A^c support.  A Gram matrix, positive semidefinite for every
K, so the symmetric pairing has no coercivity threshold at all.  It is a
different element from eq. (17)'s Petrov-Galerkin tbar^T sbar, which stays
the default (a letter in lakon(3:3)).  nasym is still raised by ncyc > 0, so
the element rides the asymmetric storage path, which stores both triangles
and factors any general matrix.

THE FORCE MUST USE THE SAME PAIRING.  resultsmech_u3.f spread the smoothed
divergence by tbar unconditionally.  The first results call builds
f = K u_prescribed, which enters the right hand side of the static solve, so
for a Galerkin stiffness the tbar spread silently dropped the symmetric
boundary coupling.  Measured at n = 4, K/G = 100, single phase, MMS: H1
1.0286 against the prototype's 0.479, while a dump of the assembled matrix
matched the prototype to 3.3e-12.  With the sbar spread the same run gives
H1 4.7936e-01 and L2 3.1960e-01, the prototype values exactly, and the PG
path is unchanged (H1 3.0944e-01).

  e_c3d_u3.f        '_' marker, dense sbar^T sbar assembly
  resultsmech_u3.f  matching internal force (sbar spread)
  mafillsmas.f      '_' -> nring = nope
  mastruct.c        skip the decode, leave nring = nope

